<title>NETHERLANDS: Ahold up after results, share split.</title>
<headline>Ahold up after results, share split.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch supermarkets group Ahold NV were up 4.40 guilders to 136.60 after the company announced full-year 1996 net profits of 632.4 million guilders and a three for one share split.</p>
<p>The result was in line with market expectations, falling within the analyst forecast range of 611 to 641 million guilders and was a 39 percent increase on 1995's 456.6 million.</p>
<p>Ahold said it expected earnings per share and consolidated result after taxes to be significantly higher in 1997.</p>
<p>The shares hit a high of 139.00 guilders before easing back.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
